    "title": "A constructed testbed for the six row types and the verdict rule",
    "description": "A small constructed book, not a measurement of any library. It drives every row type and every verdict family: a reference comparison that exceeds, a stated-domain row that is met over its domain, a consistency row, an exactness row, a vacuity row, an evidence-absent row, a not-carried row and a not-judged row. The exit status is 1 because the constructed reference row, the vacuity row and the absent row fail.",
    "library": {"name": "constructed", "version": "1"},
    "created": "2026-11-09",
    "provenance": {
      "note": "The data are synthetic and the sentences are written for this testbed. The anchor source is anchors/row-types.md."
    }
  },
  "defaults": {"root": "."},
